  "conclusions": {
    "batch_concentration": "Interactive batch/loop speedup grows monotonically as measured common H_alpha falls: 1.86× → 4.51× → 17.60× → 65.39×. Dense is not monotonic because it dips from 20.90× at H=11.994 to 15.84× at H=7.995, then rises to 56.19× and 344.87×; its endpoint advantage nevertheless grows by more than an order of magnitude.",
    "dense_vs_interactive": "Dense batch throughput is higher only at the uniform/high-entropy endpoint: 20,344.0 vs 16,827.1 ranges/s at H=11.994. As access concentrates, interactive overtakes dense between H=11.994 and H=7.995, and remains ahead at H=7.995, 4.002 and 2.001. No measured lower-entropy point has dense re-overtaking interactive."
